# Environment variables

Copy to `.env` for local development. On Vercel, set the same keys in Project → Settings → Environment Variables (Production).

## Required for client portal (production)

| Variable | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `DATABASE_URL` | Neon/Postgres connection string (portal data, magic links, sessions) |
| `JWT_SECRET` | Signs session cookies — use a long random secret |
| `RESEND_API_KEY` | Sends magic-link emails via Resend |
| `APP_URL` | Public site origin for magic-link URLs, e.g. `https://hopstecinnovation.com` |

## Recommended

| Variable | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `EMAIL_ADMIN` | Inbox for contact/inquiry notifications (default `hk@hopstecinnovation.com`) |
| `NODE_ENV` | Set to `production` on Vercel (usually automatic) |

## Optional / legacy

| Variable | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `OAUTH_SERVER_URL` | Legacy Manus OAuth — leave unset; portal uses magic links |
| `VITE_OAUTH_PORTAL_URL` | Client-side OAuth portal — leave unset |
| `VITE_APP_ID` | Legacy OAuth app id — leave unset |
| `APP_ID` | Legacy app id (defaults exist; not needed for magic links) |

## Local example

```bash
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@host/db?sslmode=require
JWT_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-string
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxx
APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
EMAIL_ADMIN=hk@hopstecinnovation.com
```

See [docs/PORTAL_PRODUCTION.md](docs/PORTAL_PRODUCTION.md) for the production go-live checklist.
